# The first vertical slice

I would begin with only:

```text
Ambuda TEI
→ STAM import
→ one root text and commentary
→ Heritage/Vidyut/DCS morphology candidates
→ commentary-intervention annotations
→ nanopublication export
→ Lean integrity certificate
```

No Neo4j. No custom corpus database. No GraphRAG. No universal ontology.

The first demonstration should answer:

> Can we import an existing Sanskrit text and commentary, annotate exactly what each commentary statement does, preserve competing readings, publish accepted claims with provenance, and mechanically certify that nothing points to missing or undeclared evidence?

After that:

```text
Tesserae adapter
→ textual reuse

STAM-Translate
→ translation comparison

AIF adapter
→ argument reconstruction
```

That is the cleanest version of the vision: **existing scholarly infrastructure underneath, Sanskritree vocabularies and adjudication in the middle, Lean certificates on top.**

